		Layla studies your face, as if listening for the part you didn't say out loud.
		do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
		Layla: Oh... right. You two don't really get along.
		do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
		do actor_change("Fiona", "shrug")
		Player: Ding-ding-ding.
		Player: Anyway, what the hell. Sure.
		Player: We'll ask him, I guess.
	else
		do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
		Layla: Fiona, what about someone from the Biochem lab?
		Layla: I imagine the departments cross-collaborate a lot, don't they?
		do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
		Layla: Surely someone from there must know something, right?
		do actor_change("Layla", "explaining")
		do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
		Player: Well, there's one guy from that department who's entered our lab multiple times to talk to Professor Greene.
		Player: He doesn't usually come around at this hour.
		Player: And anyway, he visits us infrequently.
		Player: Not a high chance he was in here yesterday evening.
		do actor_change("Layla", "talking")
		Layla: Oh. I see.
		do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
		Player: Regardless, if he is around, I suppose we could ask him about it.
		do actor_change("Fiona", "shy")
		Player: Even though I'd rather not.
		do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
		Layla: You'll see.
		do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
	do party_unhuddle()
	# step 2.404: and again, turning back to him after talking about Julian
	do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
	do actor_change("Jayce", "talk")
	Jayce: Well, glad I could help you ladies with that.
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
do actor_change("Jayce", "base")
do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
Player: Right. Thanks.
